      "side": 1,
      "message": "If only the secretmem part stays, would you mind updating the subject and body to match? Maybe something like \"ANDROID: P3S: mm: secretmem: Raise SIGBUS for 4KB pages past EOF\".\n\nCould the body also say what fails without it, in terms of 4KB processes rather than \"4K\" and \"P3S shmem slice\"? For example: a 4KB process that truncates a `memfd_secret()` file to 4KB and maps 16KB reads zeroes at offsets 4KB to 16KB instead of getting `SIGBUS`, because `secretmem_fault()` only checks the 16KB page index. It could also mention that this matches what aosp/4312526 does for `filemap_fault()` and `shmem_fault()`.",
