      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that `secretmem_fault()` needs the slice check: a `memfd_secret()` file can be truncated to any byte size, and the old check only looks at the 16KB page index, so a 4KB process can map the 4KB pages past EOF in the last 16KB page instead of getting `SIGBUS`. That is the case aosp/4312526 fixed for `filemap_fault()` and `shmem_fault()`.\n\nWould you mind reusing `vma_slice_past_eof()` here, as those two do? It keeps the native check as it is:\n\n```\n\tif (((loff_t)vmf-\u003epgoff \u003c\u003c PAGE_SHIFT) \u003e\u003d i_size_read(inode) ||\n\t    vma_slice_past_eof(vmf-\u003evma, vmf-\u003eaddress, inode))\n\t\treturn vmf_error(-EINVAL);\n```\n\n`mm/internal.h` already includes `p3s/filemap.h`, and `\u003clinux/mm.h\u003e` brings in `\u003clinux/p3s/vma.h\u003e`, so the new include could go too.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "f4c92dc437faa5b4b3f43ced61244413706121c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
