      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T22:24:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like this repeats the check just above it: `vma_slice_past_eof()` (`mm/p3s/filemap.h`, from aosp/4312526) is exactly `vma_is_p3s_4k(vma) \u0026\u0026 vma_file_offset_at(vma, addr) \u003e\u003d i_size_read(inode)`, and `shmem_fault()` already returns `VM_FAULT_SIGBUS` when it\u0027s true.\n\nAs far as I can see, no other shmem path maps a slice past EOF in a 4KB VMA either: `should_fault_around()` returns false for 4KB VMAs, so `filemap_map_pages()` isn\u0027t used there, and `vma_can_userfault()` refuses shmem userfaultfd in 4KB processes (aosp/4312484).\n\nWould it be OK to drop the `mm/shmem.c` hunk?",
